@#!/bin/bash
##------------------------------
## generate CPP server list in list.{env}.hosts
## from backend/data/list.allvms
##------------------------------

hostname pattern: ****-****-****

env	pattern
dev	****-d*cp-x***
pp      ****-ppcp-x***
prod	****-prcp-x***
q1 	****-qacp-x*** or ****-q1cp-x***
q2      ****-q2cp-x***
st      ****-stcp-x***
test    ****-tecp-x***
uat	****-u1cp-x***

linux   ****-****-x***
cpp     ****-**cp-x***

-------------------------------------------------------------
input file: $BACKEND_DIR/data/list.allvms
$ cat $BACKEND_DIR/data/list.allvms |grep -i "cp-x" |head -3
Dev - LNOC-D5CP-XCA101 (Ub) 75754650728085
Dev - LNOC-D5CP-XCA202 (Ub) 75754660300194
Dev - LNOC-D5CP-XCA303 (Ub) 75754660300195

in this file, the VM name could be upper or lower case. 

the 1-4 columns is the VM name. the hostname is the 3rd column but in lower case. 
for example, the 1st one above, the hostname is lnoc-d5cp-xca101
the hostname consist of 3 section. 1st and 2nd sections are 4 characters/numbers. the 3rd section could be 4-5 characters/numbers.
-------------------------------------------------------------

task of the script:
for each env, generate a list of the hostnames. filename: list.{env}.hosts
example: 
$ head -3 list.uat.hosts
fnoc-u1cp-xca101
fnoc-u1cp-xca102
fnoc-u1cp-xca103

-------------------------------------------------------------
